{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:75f56e8f22b64ca4","name":"System Operator","source":{"id":"source:reference-75f56e8f22b64ca4","title":"System Operator","revision":18548,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:17:59Z","sha256":"654b28612cc059e1425b821ceb723fa157de5fa56fbbc168ef697d540a88053f","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18548","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=System%20Operator&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-75f56e8f22b64ca4","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Core Rulebook"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Core_Rulebook"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The System Operator manages the Vehicle's shields, sensors, and communications. A ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," can have only one System Operator at a time. \n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The below Actions include all other Actions that can be performed while functioning as a System Operator:\n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Actions"}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Aid Another"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},", you can aid an ally's next skill check or attack roll, or you can interfere with an enemy's attacks.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Aiding a Skill Check"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["You can help another character achieve success on their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Check"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ability Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ability_Check"}," by making the same kind of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Check"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ability Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ability_Check"}," in a cooperative effort. If you roll a 10 or higher on your check, the character you are helping receives a +2 bonus on their own check. You can't ",{"tag":"a","children":["Take 10"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Take_10"}," on a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Skill Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Skill_Check"}," or ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ability Check"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ability_Check"}," to Aid Another.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Aiding an Attack Roll"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["In combat, you can Aid Another character's attack by forcing an opponent to avoid your own attacks, making it more difficult for them to avoid your ally. Select an opponent and make an attack against a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of 10. If you succeed, you grant a +2 bonus on a single ally's next attack roll against that opponent.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["In ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Combat"},", you can Aid Another character's attack by providing improved targeting data, or by coordinating that Attack with other Vehicle Actions.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"ul","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["A System Operator can grant a +2 bonus on another character's attack roll by making a DC 10 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check."]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Suppressing an Enemy"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["In combat, you can distract or interfere with an opponent, making their attacks more difficult. Select an opponent and make an attack against a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"}," of 10. If you succeed, that opponent takes a -2 penalty on its next attack roll.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Melee Attacks"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["With a melee weapon, you can strike any opponent within a square you ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threaten"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threaten"},". You can only ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threaten"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threaten"}," squares within your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reach"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reach"}," from the Vehicle's space, and you don't ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threaten"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threaten"}," spaces around the Vehicle at all if it grants ",{"tag":"a","children":["Total Cover"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Total_Cover"},". You can't make a melee attack in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},", except within the confines of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," you occupy.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For example, a Jedi on a Speeder Bike could attack targets adjacent to the bike with their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Lightsaber"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Lightsaber","referenceId":"reference:987a817de9003439"},", but the same Jedi couldn't do so while inside an ",{"tag":"a","children":["AT-AT"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/AT-AT","referenceId":"reference:72b76e7d76526ae5"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Ranged Attacks"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["With a ranged weapon, you can throw or shoot at any target within your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Line of Sight"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Line_of_Sight","referenceId":"reference:7ae5eaf79143552f"},", as long as your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," does not grant you ",{"tag":"a","children":["Total Cover"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Total_Cover"}," (",{"tag":"a","children":["Range"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Range"}," modifiers apply normally for your weapon). You cannot make a personal ranged attack in ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},", except within the confines of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," you occupy.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For example, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Clone Troopers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Clone_Troopers"}," can fire their blasters at targets outside a ",{"tag":"a","children":["LAAT/i Gunship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/LAAT/i_Gunship","referenceId":"reference:4ec307279de7b7a7"},", as long as the ship's doors are open.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Intercept Communications"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},", you can attempt to Intercept Communications between two other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},". If the other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," take no special precautions, this is a DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check; otherwise, the DC is set by the higher of their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check results for securing communications (see ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Communications"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Communications","referenceId":"reference:fa12b21dc3aa7266"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Furthermore, if the other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"}," are using encrypted communications systems (such as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Comlink"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Comlink","referenceId":"reference:609e72c37493843f"}," (Encrypted) or ",{"tag":"a","children":["IFF Transponders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/IFF_Transponders"}," with matching encryption codes), add 10 to the DC. If your check result fails by 10 or less when attempting to intercept encrypted communications, you can identify what encryption protocols they are using. (\"It might be an Imperial Code.\")\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Use Sensors"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Standard Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Standard_Action"},", a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check lets a System Operator hear or see other targets or detect someone or something sneaking up on them from behind. If the target is actively attempting to remain undetected, your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check is opposed by the target's ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stealth"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stealth","referenceId":"reference:526a40a447ddd7aa"}," check. If the target is not making any special effort to avoid detection, the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check DC is determined by the target's size:\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["TARGET SIZE\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["DC\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Colossal\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-15\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Gargantuan\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-10\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Huge\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["-5\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":["Large\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["0\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["On ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"}," maps, your ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check has a -5 penalty for every 10 squares between you and the target, and you take a -5 penalty on your check if attempting to detect a target that is powered down or otherwise not emitting an energy signature. Obstacles, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Cloaking Devices"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Cloaking_Devices"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jamming Suites"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jamming_Suites"},", and sensor masks can also impose penalties.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Move Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Actions"}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Search Starship"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["A System Operator may attempt to learn more about a target by making a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check (taking a -5 penalty for every 10 squares between you and the target at ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship Scale"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship_Scale"},"). A DC 10 check result identifies the size of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," and determines whether it has shields active. A DC 15 check result reveals the exact make of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," (if the observer would recognize it- alien ships are simply identified as being of unknown manufacture) and the number of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Weapons"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Weapons"}," it has (but not the exact type of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Weapon Systems"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Weapon_Systems"},").\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The first time a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," moves within 30 squares of yours, you may make a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"}," to identify it. Further efforts require a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},".\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Actions"}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Raise or Lower Shields"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["By spending a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},", a System Operator can activate or deactivate the shields on their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"},". Shields are generally kept inactive in noncombat situations to reduce strain on the Vehicle's systems, and Raising Shields is often perceived as evidence of hostile intent, so many ",{"tag":"a","children":["Commanders"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Commanders"}," prefer to keep their shields down, unless they are expecting trouble.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Recharge Shields"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["By spending 3 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Actions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Actions"}," during the same turn, or on consecutive turns, a System Operator can make a DC 20 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mechanics"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mechanics","referenceId":"reference:1c74a0e2ceaaeb28"}," check to increase their Vehicle's current ",{"tag":"a","children":["Shield Rating"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Shield_Rating"}," by 5, up to its normal maximum.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Use Communications"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["As a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Swift Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Swift_Action"},", a System Operator can make a DC 5 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check to hail a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," (DC 0 if the other ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," is using an ",{"tag":"a","children":["IFF Transponder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/IFF_Transponder"}," with the same encryption codes as yours); if willing, that Vehicle's ","System Operator"," can then open communications as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"},". You can also attempt to establish secure communications, but doing this requires both System Operators to make a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Move Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Move_Action"},". The greater of the two check results sets the DC for any attempts to intercept their communications.\n"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reactions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reactions"}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Avoid Surprise"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["In ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle_Combat"},", a System Operator makes a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check at the start of a battle to determine whether or not they are ",{"tag":"a","children":["Surprised"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Surprised"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Detect Hyperspace Travel"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["When a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"}," enters or exits hyperspace, it produces a short burst of Cronau radiation. Any ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starship"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Station"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Station"},", or sensor array within the same star system can detect a Cronau radiation burst with a DC 25 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check made as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Reaction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reaction"},". Success indicates that the ","System Operator"," detects the ship entering or exiting hyperspace, and is aware of it's point of arrival or departure. Tracking a ship through hyperspace also relies on the presence of residual Cronau radiation.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Taking a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Full-Round Action"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Full-Round_Action"}," to make a DC 25 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check measures the amount of Cronau radiation as well as the angle of departure of the vessel fleeing into hyperspace, indicating the most likely destination. Cronau radiation lingers for several hours after a ship has fled into hyperspace, though each hour since the ship made the jump to lightspeed increases the DC of the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check by 5.\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
